{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1370","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Odd-Even Subsequence"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ashish has an array $$$a$$$ of size $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A subsequence of $$$a$$$ is defined as a sequence that can be obtained from $$$a$$$ by deleting some elements (possibly none), without changing the order of the remaining elements."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider a subsequence $$$s$$$ of $$$a$$$. He defines the cost of $$$s$$$ as the minimum between: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The maximum among all elements at odd indices of $$$s$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The maximum among all elements at even indices of $$$s$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that the index of an element is its index in $$$s$$$, rather than its index in $$$a$$$. The positions are numbered from $$$1$$$. So, the cost of $$$s$$$ is equal to $$$min(max(s_1, s_3, s_5, \\ldots), max(s_2, s_4, s_6, \\ldots))$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, the cost of $$$\\{7, 5, 6\\}$$$ is $$$min( max(7, 6), max(5) ) = min(7, 5) = 5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Help him find the minimum cost of a subsequence of size $$$k$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$2 \\leq k \\leq n \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$)  — the size of the array $$$a$$$ and the size of the subsequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq a_i \\leq 10^9$$$)  — the elements of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a single integer  — the minimum cost of a subsequence of size $$$k$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 2\n1 2 3 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 3\n1 2 3 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5 3\n5 3 4 2 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6 4\n5 3 50 2 4 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test, consider the subsequence $$$s$$$ = $$$\\{1, 3\\}$$$. Here the cost is equal to $$$min(max(1), max(3)) = 1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test, consider the subsequence $$$s$$$ = $$$\\{1, 2, 4\\}$$$. Here the cost is equal to $$$min(max(1, 4), max(2)) = 2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fourth test, consider the subsequence $$$s$$$ = $$$\\{3, 50, 2, 4\\}$$$. Here the cost is equal to $$$min(max(3, 2), max(50, 4)) = 3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1370D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1370/problem/D"}